  "observations": [
    "Coarse DEM anchor89.70m, hillside tower64.24m: relative drop25.46m agrees approximately with provisional court25 versus hillside tower0, but does not establish footings.",
    "Castle corners span coarse79.92–94.35m while architectural court is flat. The main walls/towers can still float or embed on this smooth DEM.",
    "Museum-north90.20m versus museum-south75.87m:14.33m descent under a single modeled floor. The real ledge/retaining section or independent wing levels must be resolved; do not flatten the ground to disguise this.",
    "DGT public viewer query111–112m differs substantially from the coarse DEM and the historical operator observatory111.229m absolute altitude. These are separate observations; no source is silently converted into a relative tower height.",
    "DGT public catalog exposes MDT50cm/2m descriptions but marks the raster collections access private and license proprietary. Bulk acquisition was not attempted. Official open-data policy refers to CC-BY4.0; authenticated download/license clarification may provide the required precise ground controls."
  ],
  "limitations": "Research preview only.25m interpolated sample spacing is not a25m survey; underlying mixed DEM sources are coarser and may miss terraces/cliffs/buildings. Hill stays separate from all runtime GLBs. No local ground flattening or added retaining walls. Geographic/fidelity approval and physical terrain alignment remain pending."
